# Week 2 Report: Financial Statement Analysis and Valuation Modeling

**Company studied:** Microsoft Corporation (NASDAQ: MSFT), fiscal years 2024 to 2026

**Prepared by:** Nayana Sheelavant        **Date:** 19th October, 2026

## 1. Introduction and Choice of Company

Week 1 ended with a plan for studying the technology sector, so this week I picked one company from it and went through its numbers properly. I chose Microsoft. It is one of the largest listed companies in the world, it sits in the software and cloud part of the sector I wrote about, and its latest annual results came out only in late July, so the data is fresh. Microsoft's fiscal year runs from 1 July to 30 June, which means FY2026 covers July 2025 to June 2026.

The aim is straightforward. I want to read the income statement, balance sheet and cash flow statement together, decide how healthy the business really is, and then build a basic valuation to see whether a share price of $529.05 (the 16 October 2026 close) looks reasonable. Everything is in US dollars. Where I had to make a judgement call, I say so in the text.

