### 8.6 What the share price implies

I also ran the model backwards. Keeping my base-case operating forecast, the current price of $529.05 is justified only if the discount rate is about 8.6%, which is well below the 9.9% I built from today's yields. Alternatively, keeping the 9.9% discount rate, the price needs revenue to grow about 31% faster than my base case in every year. Put differently, the market is paying for something close to my bull case, or it is using a lower discount rate than I am.

